WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.818
Please welcome Navyn Salem.

2
00:00:02.818 --> 00:00:05.818
(audience cheering)

3
00:00:09.966 --> 00:00:14.966
I'm very honored to meet you, I really love your story.

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.790
How did you end up on this trip in the first place?

5
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:22.410
So, I mean, really the reason behind it is my dad,

6
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.510 line:15%
and he's from Tanzania, along with my grandparents

7
00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:26.390 line:15%
and great grandparents.

8
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.870 line:15%
So we have a long family history in East Africa.

9
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.240 line:15%
And also at the same time,

10
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.430
my daughters were all about under the age of five.

11
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.570
And so I packed my bags one day and went to

12
00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.080
Dar Es Salaam, Tanzania,

13
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.130
to see what was going on in the world.

14
00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.360
And wanted to see like what's missing,

15
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.620
what needs to be done, what action needs to be taken.

16
00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.340
And I started to learn about malnutrition

17
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:53.030
and understood that 8,000 children a day

18
00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:56.630
were dying from something that is 100% preventable,

19
00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.540
which is hunger and malnutrition.

20
00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.770
So just looking into my own daughter's eyes, right,

21
00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.870
and understanding that mothers every single day

22
00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.130
are losing their children

23
00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.730
to something that we know how to treat.

24
00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.710
And I really felt that urgency,

25
00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:13.660
