28
00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.490 line:15%
and it kept me up at night.

29
00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.910 line:15%
And I knew that I had do something about it

30
00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.800 line:15%
and I didn't have any experience,

31
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.900 line:15%
I had never worked for a nonprofit before,

32
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.260
I have no manufacturing experience, nothing.

33
00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.840
But I was like, if we don't do something

34
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.670
then lives are at stake.

35
00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.060
And this is an opportunity and a responsibility

36
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.960
to do something at that moment and take action.

37
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.022
I mean-

38
00:01:40.022 --> 00:01:42.455
(audience applauds)

39
00:01:42.455 --> 00:01:45.933
Where did you, you go, like, where did you start?

40
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.980
Did people take you seriously?

41
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:53.760
What was your first lesson that we could all learn from?

42
00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:54.593
Yeah, I mean,

43
00:01:54.593 --> 00:01:56.560
I traveled with a bunch of different nonprofits

44
00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.810
and I learned about their philosophies, their mandates,

45
00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.100
how they worked and I came home and I said,

46
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.010
I wanna do this completely differently.

47
00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.030
I remember having a follow up call with them and saying,

48
00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:08.070
I have this idea to start a business but it's a nonprofit,

49
00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:09.640
